&lt;li value=&quot;3&quot;&gt;Experience owning technical problems end to end, making sound architectural trade-offs, and guiding other engineers through code reviews and mentorship.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;4&quot;&gt;Clear written and spoken English communication skills and comfort working in a fully remote, largely asynchronous environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;5&quot;&gt;Alignment with GitLab&#39;s values and commitment to an inclusive culture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;6&quot;&gt;Experience with IDE extension development, such as JetBrains plugins in Kotlin or VS Code extensions, and understanding of the Language Server Protocol (LSP), language servers, or editor integrations are helpful but not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our broader Developer Clients group includes the VS Code and JetBrains functional teams. We hold a weekly sync and encourage engineers to collaborate across team boundaries when it benefits the shared developer experience. We&#39;re fully remote and work largely asynchronously, partnering closely with Product, Design, and engineering teams across AI Clients to align on long-term architecture and deliver iterative improvements.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How GitLab Supports Full-Time Employees&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
